92186045585 true] [17592186407348 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(1,0,-1)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(1,0)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,0) & =1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 0}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1,0)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(1,0)}(y-0) \\\\ z-(-1) & =(-1)y \\\\ z & =-y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,0,-1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ z=-y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533540 17592186045585 true] [17592186407349 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407351 13194139533540 17592186045585 true] [17592186407349 1062 #uuid "8482a7f1-9b85-58c1-b946-6953c47668a6" 13194139533540 17592186045585 true] [17592186407349 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407348 13194139533540 17592186045585 true] [17592186407350 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407349 13194139533540 17592186045585 true] [17592186407350 1062 #uuid "e1916473-66ad-5022-aafa-9787da440dac" 13194139533540 17592186045585 true] [17592186407350 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125189 13194139533540 17592186045585 true] [17592186407351 1062 #uuid "f2c84ac0-3b38-584c-9809-dfa6181b9351" 13194139533540 17592186045585 true] [17592186407351 1063 #edb/ref 17592186338923 13194139533540 17592186045585 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-f13d4530-1c8e-598a-986b-9b8f2a13e396" 17592186407335 "answer-25cf98fa-a5b3-5e6b-b710-84fa1db64ec9" 17592186407336 "answer-3f49be2f-9fbd-57d9-8743-c7f792e14929" 17592186407337 "answer-40205211-9c82-5bbc-b29c-5211d1a45bbb" 17592186407338 "answer-5de2add0-6423-5754-a07f-96730ef51cc3" 17592186407339 "answer-645649e7-f6ca-5dcf-a129-028646be2cfe" 17592186407340 "answer-8d3f